# The words an ask may use

{{ wrap 80 "How a sound should be, in the words a person would use. These are what a ToneSpec's `words` field carries, and the only ones it carries: a word outside this list is reported and moves nothing, rather than being refused, because refusing an ask over a word would make the format hostile to the person it exists for." }}

{{ wrap 80 (printf "%d words on %d axes. %d of those axes move a control when a preset is built and %d describe the player and the instrument, which no amplifier, reverb or compressor has a control for." .Words (len .Axes) .Acting .Describing) }}

## Describe the result, not the control

{{ wrap 80 "\"mid-forward\", never \"raise the mids\". Where the treble knob sits is a fact about somebody's amplifier; how the record came out is a fact about the sound, and only the second survives being read on other gear. That is why a knob position is never written in an ask." }}

## One word per axis

{{ wrap 80 "An axis is a question, and the words on it are answers that exclude each other. Saying `mid-forward` has already said `not scooped`, so an ask claiming both has claimed nothing: apply them in turn and the control lands where it started. A build reports an axis answered twice and moves neither." }}

{{ wrap 80 "A word that would answer two axes at once cannot be written yet. \"Punchy\" is the obvious one, meaning both a bottom that stops when the note does and a front of the note you can hear. Nothing structural forbids it. What is missing is how to divide one word's step between two controls, and nobody has measured that." }}

## Evidence decides how far a word moves

{{ wrap 80 "A word carries its own evidence, and that is not decoration. How far it moves a control is sized from how far that word's own measurement sits from every other rig's, so a word measured close to the pack barely moves anything and a word nobody measured takes the whole step. It is the difference between a knob moved because somebody listened and a knob moved because a model guessed." }}

{{ wrap 80 "One word is one opinion, so no word moves a control more than a quarter of its range whatever its evidence says." }}
